<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Castro</h1><p class="st-meta">1537 CE – 1649 CE · capital Castro</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Farnese duchy in northern Lazio created by Pope Paul III for his son, whose capital was razed by a later pope in 1649.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1537 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-paul-iii">Pope Paul III</a>, born Alessandro Farnese, carved the Duchy of Castro out of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/papal-states">Papal States</a> for his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pier-luigi-farnese">Pier Luigi Farnese</a>. It covered the old Farnese estates between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-bolsena">Lake Bolsena</a> and the Tyrrhenian coast.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Castro was rebuilt as a small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> capital, with buildings by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-da-sangallo-the-younger">Antonio da Sangallo the Younger</a>. After 1545 its dukes were also dukes of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-parma-and-piacenza">Duchy of Parma and Piacenza</a>, and they ran Castro from afar, borrowing heavily against it. A quarrel over these debts and the Farnese's power led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-urban-viii">Pope Urban VIII</a> to fight the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-war-of-castro">First War of Castro</a> in 1641–1644, which ended in a papal setback.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1649, after the murder of the new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of Castro was blamed on the Farnese, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-innocent-x">Pope Innocent X's</a> troops took the town and razed it to the ground. The duchy was absorbed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/papal-states">Papal States</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-castro.jpg" alt="Duchy of Castro" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Lexicon · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Duchy_of_Parma.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1537 CE – 1649 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Castro</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Pier Luigi Farnese, Odoardo Farnese, Ranuccio II Farnese</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Italian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Castro</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1593&amp;focus=duchy-of-castro" aria-label="Duchy of Castro on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4962 666 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Castro lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5282 922L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5282 922h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5282 922h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1593&amp;focus=duchy-of-castro">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

